<item><title>Six workers dead as eight-storey building collapses near Nairobi</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/six-workers-dead-as-eight-storey-building-collapses-near-5740b5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/six-workers-dead-as-eight-storey-building-collapses-near-5740b5/</guid><category>Kenya</category><description>All 405 workers at the site have been accounted for, but the cause is still under investigation, with formwork failure suspected.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:35:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ke.jpg" length="31123" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ke.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Kenya holds fuel pump prices with Sh4.6bn subsidy</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-holds-fuel-pump-prices-with-sh4-6bn-subsidy-f6ea72/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-holds-fuel-pump-prices-with-sh4-6bn-subsidy-f6ea72/</guid><category>Kenya</category><description>The Energy and Petroleum Regulatory Authority says pump prices will not change for 30 days even though the cost of all three fuels rose between September and October.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:32:14 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-holds-fuel-pump-prices-with-sh4-6bn-subsidy-f6ea72/share.jpg" length="38749" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-holds-fuel-pump-prices-with-sh4-6bn-subsidy-f6ea72/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mathare residents clear river debris ahead of El Niño rains</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/mathare-residents-clear-river-debris-ahead-of-el-nino-rains-255ab1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/mathare-residents-clear-river-debris-ahead-of-el-nino-rains-255ab1/</guid><category>Kenya</category><description>Kenya&apos;s Meteorological Service has warned of potentially intense rainfall between October and December, and residents are clearing their riverside settlement.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:42:14 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ke.jpg" length="31123" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ke.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
